Equation Listing    SOLVE Shipment Using LP From line 81


---- objective  =E=  equation representing objective function

objective..  4*x(KansasCity,Minneapolis) + 12*x(KansasCity,NewYork) + 18*x(KansasCity,SanFrancisco) + 18*x(KansasCity,Seattle) + 9*x(Dallas,Minneapolis) + 15*x(Dallas,NewYork) + 17*x(Dallas,SanFrancisco) + 21*x(Dallas,Seattle) - z =E= 0 ; (LHS = 0)
     

---- supplyConstraint  =L=  equation representing supply constraint

supplyConstraint(KansasCity)..  x(KansasCity,Minneapolis) + x(KansasCity,NewYork) + x(KansasCity,SanFrancisco) + x(KansasCity,Seattle) =L= 1000 ; (LHS = 0)
     
supplyConstraint(Dallas)..  x(Dallas,Minneapolis) + x(Dallas,NewYork) + x(Dallas,SanFrancisco) + x(Dallas,Seattle) =L= 800 ; (LHS = 0)
     

---- demandConstraint  =E=  equation representing demand constraint

demandConstraint(Minneapolis)..  x(KansasCity,Minneapolis) + x(Dallas,Minneapolis) =E= 400 ; (LHS = 0, INFES = 400 ****)
     
demandConstraint(NewYork)..  x(KansasCity,NewYork) + x(Dallas,NewYork) =E= 250 ; (LHS = 0, INFES = 250 ****)
     
demandConstraint(SanFrancisco)..  x(KansasCity,SanFrancisco) + x(Dallas,SanFrancisco) =E= 450 ; (LHS = 0, INFES = 450 ****)
     
